From f40fa069b4ce803cc2d73976b1ecde90f579bfdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy <guy.xtafcusqt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:36:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(acp): name background subagents and shell jobs by their
 description

A subagent was reported as the bare kind "subagent" and a shell job by its raw
command line, so the platform's background-work list could not tell two runs
apart without opening each one.

Subagents are now reported from the parent's subagent/catalog entry, which the
manager appends once per in-process child before the run starts and which
carries the delegating call's `description` as its label. Shell jobs are
matched by owner and exact command to the still-open call that started them,
and take that call's `description` as their name; the command line moves to
the description so it stays visible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
